Lets an Alloy-style browser's page be brought forward, for Arbalete, whose
tabs are all Alloy-style browsers: Picture in Picture's back to tab button,
`window.focus()`, a service worker's `clients.focus()` and DevTools'
Page.bringToFront all ask the page's WebContentsDelegate to ActivateContents,
which Alloy left empty. It now tells the client through
CefFocusHandler::OnSetFocus with FOCUS_SOURCE_SYSTEM, like
CefBrowserHost::SetFocus(true) does; the client selects the page's tab.

diff --git a/cef/libcef/browser/alloy/alloy_browser_host_impl.cc b/cef/libcef/browser/alloy/alloy_browser_host_impl.cc
index 248604e..4629d48 100644
--- a/cef/libcef/browser/alloy/alloy_browser_host_impl.cc
+++ b/cef/libcef/browser/alloy/alloy_browser_host_impl.cc
@@ -965,6 +965,12 @@ bool AlloyBrowserHostImpl::TakeFocus(content::WebContents* source,
   return contents_delegate_.TakeFocus(source, reverse);
 }
 
+// Asked to bring its page forward, like Picture in Picture's back to tab button
+// does, the client is told through OnSetFocus.
+void AlloyBrowserHostImpl::ActivateContents(content::WebContents* contents) {
+  OnSetFocus(FOCUS_SOURCE_SYSTEM);
+}
